            "review_title": "Review at The Coral 2",
            "review_text": "Юлия М\nTomsk, Russia10 contributions\n0\nGood , quality restaurant\nApr 2025 • Family\nA very nice restaurant. We were in Nha Trang in April 25th. We came here by accident and then we visited constantly. We ate Vietnamese and Thai cuisine, there were 6 adults with different tastes and everyone liked it!!!! We took grilled pits and shrimp and fish in butter sauce, grilled fish from a fish tank and fried and shelled mussels! The lobster was taken for the last time: delicious! Kohl's waiter cleaned them for us. The people, especially the Russian people, very many, in the evening the table was vacant had to wait. People are coming. Every time, I observed that the visitors were the same. All we drank was beer. It's not impossible to bring your own alcohol. The portions are huge, especially the first courses. A welcome shot of moonshine. The price tag is very democratic, like in Russia to eat in the Uzbek. In front of the entrance there are aquariums and the Russian called Alexander told everything according to the menu and advised what to take! Every time they chose on his advice and were very pleased! We at our hotel advised other holidaymakers of this restaurant and thanked everyone! Price and quality! Yes, it's not a fancy restaurant, but it's twice as expensive and the quality is the same. Greetings to Alexander from Siberia, Tomsk.From Vadim (8 (953) 913-44-80, Yulia , Igor and company! I recommend a visit.\nRead more\nTranslated from Russian\nShow original\nWritten April 26, 2025",
